  "id": "retinal-oscillations",
  "term": "retinal oscillations",
  "definition": "Retinal oscillations are abnormal rhythmic patterns of electrical activity in the retina that can appear after photoreceptors degenerate. In retinitis pigmentosa models, they are described as pathological rhythmic activity that may interfere with efforts to restore vision.",
